{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.QuantumIdealGasLaw","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.QuantumIdealGasLaw","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.MathConstants","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ideal_gas_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ideal_gas_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L117-L128","doc":"The full equation of state decomposes as PV = NT + N·T·correction:\nthe correction is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ideal_gas_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ideal_gas_full","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L93-L115","doc":"**Full quantum ideal gas law**: P · V = N · T_q · (1 + correction).\n\nGiven the equation of state with correction factor, the pressure-volume\nproduct decomposes into the classical part N·T_q and the q-anomaly part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ideal_gas_leading_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ideal_gas_leading_order","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L79-L91","doc":"**Leading-order quantum ideal gas law**: P · V = N · T_q.\n\nThis encodes the equation of state at zeroth order in ℏ_q.\nThe full equation includes the correction 1 + ℏ_q²⟨S_q⟩/[2]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.correctionFactor_vanishes_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.correctionFactor_vanishes_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L72-L77","doc":"The q-anomaly correction factor vanishes when ℏ_q = 0 (classicality).\nStated directly: for any q, S, the expression ℏ_q² · S / [2]_q\nvanishes when ℏ_q = 0. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.correctionFactor_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.correctionFactor_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L62-L70","doc":"The q-anomaly correction is non-negative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.correctionFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.correctionFactor","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L56-L60","doc":"The q-anomaly correction factor: ℏ_q² · ⟨S_q⟩ / [2]_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hS","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Non-negative action expectation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hV","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hV","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Positive volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.hq","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L50-L50","doc":"q > 1 (non-classical). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.boundaryNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.boundaryNorm","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Boundary norm (Frobenius pairing contribution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.meanAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.meanAction","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Thermal expectation of the categorical action ⟨S_q⟩. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.V_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.V_q","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Quantum volume V_q of the region. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.N","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Number of particle knots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.point","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.sp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.sp","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas.mk","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.IdealKnotGas","kind":"structure","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L35-L54","doc":"**Quantum ideal gas state**: the thermodynamic data of a gas of\nN non-interacting particle knots in a region with quantum volume V_q.\nLabel: prop:quantum-ideal-gas-law ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:quantum-ideal-gas-law","label":"prop:quantum-ideal-gas-law","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.quantumTemperature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.quantumTemperature","kind":"def","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L28-L33","doc":"**Quantum temperature** `T_q(p) = ℏ_q(p)`.\nThe brane is at unit thermal scale set by the quantum Planck constant\n(see `quantum-pressure.md`: `T_q = ℏ_q`, `β_q = 1/ℏ_q = t_P(q)`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:quantum-temperature","label":"def:quantum-temperature","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-temperature.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.R_q","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/quantum-ideal-gas-law.lean#L24-L26","doc":"Ground ring: archimedean specialisation `R_q := ℝ` (AGENTS.md §7c).\nThe numerical substrate value `q₀ ≈ 1.1097` lives in `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}